Local changes to the JPEG-AI reference software (commit e9648f9a4bb98d8fb7333e97d4df4f0979520a7c,
https://gitlab.com/wg1/jpeg-ai/jpeg-ai-reference-software) that the face1kb benchmark ran with.
Apply inside the checkout with `git apply` (scripts/setup_jpegai.sh does this).

* src/__init__.py: default torch.load(weights_only=False) as in torch < 2.6; the reference
  software loads full pickled checkpoints and caches.
* src/codec/entropy_coding/binarizers.py: the bypass decoder returns an array of decoded
  symbols; use its first element when decoding unary / Exp-Golomb header fields (without this
  the stored bitstreams do not decode in the paper environment).
* src/reco/coders/decoder.py: install the ptflops hooks only when --calc_ptflops is set.
* scripts/build_ec_lib.sh, scripts/build_test_libs.sh: activate a conda environment only if
  conda exists, so that the entropy-coder libraries build in any Python environment.

